From 813fa7c34ca904af6fdec79693dd475a98f63ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:36:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/70] CUDA/HIP: unrolled rms_norm*mul(+q8_1) for
 2048..8192-column rows, DPP reductions (GGML_HIP_NORM_FAST)

rms_norm_mul_f32_unrolled<NV>: thread t still owns columns t + 1024k and every sum keeps the order and pairing of
rms_norm_f32<1024, true>, but the NV loads of x and of the weight are issued up front, the block and q8_1 group
reductions use permlanex16/DPP row_xmask (warp_reduce_sum_dpp / warp_reduce_max_dpp, moved from mmvq.cu to
common.cuh) and the NV q8_1 groups of a thread are unrolled. The sum of squares is an explicit fma chain: unrolled,
tmp += x*x let the backend fuse the first product into the second add instead (1 ulp off in ~4% of rows; found
with a 2000-row bitwise harness and an in-model check).

rocprofv3 (Qwen3.8-27B, MTP n=4): rms_norm*mul 5.87 -> 4.51 us (128 per verify, 20 per draft chain: 5.63 -> 4.21).
Greedy md5 (plain and MTP) equal to 9f83f1f81; bitwise harness 2000 rows x 5120 (incl. in-place, zeros, 1e-21,
3000-scale outliers): 0 f32 and 0 q8_1 differences. test-backend-ops RMS_NORM 53/53, RMS_NORM_MUL_ADD 37/37.
GGML_HIP_NORM_FAST=0 restores rms_norm_f32<1024, true>.
